---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Your Golf Buddy"
  description="Your Golf Buddy has no accounts and collects no personal data. Your rounds are stored on your device."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16 prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Last updated {new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long" })}.</p>
    <p>
      Your Golf Buddy has no user accounts. It never asks for your name, email
      address, or a password. The rounds, courses, and notes you enter are stored
      locally on your device.
    </p>
    <h2>Cloud sync (optional, paid)</h2>
    <p>
      If you buy the Golf Buddy Pass and turn on sync, your rounds are copied to
      our server so you can use them on another device. That data is tied to a
      random identifier generated on your device, not to any personal
      information. You can delete all synced data at any time from the app's
      settings.
    </p>
    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      yourbuddy.golf is a static site. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics
      or third-party trackers.
    </p>
    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      The Golf Buddy Pass is sold through Stripe. Stripe processes your payment
      details; we never see your card number. See Stripe's privacy policy for how
      they handle that data.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about your data: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
